{
  "id": 22,
  "name": "cluster_hub_v1",
  "intent": "Prefer candidates that are local hubs of unvisited cities (high cluster_density) with uniform neighborhood distances (low spread), while staying close to current position. Hypothesis: cluster interiors are traversed cheaply when entered, so picking hubs first exploits density before paying long inter-cluster jumps; spread penalty avoids edge nodes with uneven neighbor profiles.",
